abstract: >
  HyCAN-DB is an open database of primary hydrogen sorption measurements on
  carbon sorbents, built under a publicly registered protocol: 17,061
  measurement rows from 124 papers (1987-2026), 80 of them a stratified
  probability sample of a 5,251-record frame, each independently
  dual-extracted and adjudicated, with released agreement statistics, a
  60-row author audit, and registered design-based analyses of the Chahine
  rule, interlaboratory precision, reporting practice and prediction
  baselines. Data CC BY 4.0; code MIT.
repository-code: "https://github.com/AvinGupta-ship-it/hycan-db"
keywords:
  - hydrogen storage
  - carbon nanomaterials
  - adsorption
  - Chahine rule
  - systematic review
  - probability sample
  - FAIR data
